een able  to change as the world changes and  because despite our differences we are  united in our commitment to each other  NATO is an alliance over sovereign  nations united by democracy liberty and  the rule of law by a person's right to  live their life in the pursuit of  happiness free from oppression values  that lie at the heart of the United  States and at the heart of NATO as  President Eisenhower NATO's first  supreme Allied commander said we are  concerned not only with the protection  of territory but with the defense of a  way of life Europe and North America are  not separated by the Atlantic Ocean we  are united by it and just like Atlantic  NATO unites our continents our nations  and our people it has done so for 70  years and today we must do everything in  our power to maintain that unity for  future generations because combat may we  are stronger and safer when we stand  together madam speaker mr. vice  president it is good to have friends  [Applause]  [Applause]
 

